#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# acot

#% text
# `acot(z)` gives the inverse cotangent.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For complex `z` the principal value is `atan(1/z)`.

#% item
# Exact special values and odd symmetry are applied; other exact arguments stay unevaluated.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
acot(1)
#% output
#= (1/4)*pi

#% cell
acot(0.5)
#% output
#= 1.1071487177940904

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
acot(-x)
#% output
#= -acot(x)

#% text
# 30 digits:

#% cell
n(acot(1/3), 30)
#% output
#= 1.249045772398254425829917077281090

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `log`, `atan`, `asin`, `acos`
